{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design","id":1550127,"title":"Nosferatu Warren Design","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-14T17:06:25-07:00","id":1550127,"title":"Nosferatu Warren Design","content":"I will probably be having a Nosferatu as one of the PCs in my upcoming chronicle so I wanted to give some thoughts to actual design of the local warrens. It's been a long time since I last had a Nosferatu PC, and back then I handwaved a lot of things. Now I want to get into some of the actual details of the clan as shown in the Players Guides and Clanbooks.<br /> <br /> The Clanbooks only mention a few basic design elements.<br /> <br /> There's an <b>antechamber</b>; a room or rooms where non-clan visitors are brought to wait to ask favors from the Nosferatu if the clan really wants to make them earn it. It can typically only be accessed through a series of confusing mazes filled with cramped tunnels, vermin, and traps. It's part defense to discourage unwelcome visitors and part torment to evaluate the visitor before deciding to grant his request.<br /> <br /> Then deep within the war there is the <b>chamber of horror</b>, basically a very large meeting room that can hold all the clan's members. It's supposed to be the most defensible place in the warrens. Presumably it is the place of &quot;final battle&quot; if the clan finds itself under attack. When the local brood meets in a Hosting, it's supposed to be the responsible of the Nosferatu who called it to provide the meeting place. So the chamber of horrors is not the place where the clan meets per se, although I do imagine individual Nosferatu do decide that is the place where they'll be meeting. But that's only an option, not a requirement.<br /> <br /> Then there's a place for a <b>spawning pool</b>, a place of fresh water that the eldest Nosferatu provide vitae so they can create various fearsome ghouled animals who will be part of the warren's defenses.<br /> <br /> Not mentioned are any lairs for individual Nosferatu who want an actual place to slumber during the day or hideout in general. I assume they are there though.<br /> <br /> Everything else can just be consigned to the categories of &quot;traps&quot;, dead ends, or other defenses.<br /> <br /> Do people have any examples of traps, interesting flavor text, drawn maps, curiosities, or other design elements they'd like to share? Curious as to how people run or design the warrens in specific ways, especially in regards to making it an interesting roleplayinh experience for Nosferatu PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T17:14:17-07:00","id":1550130,"title":"","content":"Also interested in people's opinions on including more outlandish elements associated with the warrens. <br /> <br /> The Animalism level six power Song in the Dark allows the Nosferatu to summon what is explicitly an underground dwelling monster of the underworld. Presumably this could be anything from a fomori, monster, bygone, creature from the Dreaming, or some underground umbral realm. I've never actually seen this power use, but it's mentioned in both clanbooks. Has anyone actually seen this used? If so, was it used for anything other than providing yet another creature to fight against intruders in the warrens?<br /> <br /> Similarly, has anyone ever used a plot of something hunting Nosferatu in the warrens? Or at least a mysterious, unknown creature the Nosferatu believe is there, but don't know what it is? If so, what did you use? What complications happened? How was it kept fun and entertaining?<br /> <br /> I'm looking for other elements that I could use for the place than just having a &quot;safe spot&quot; for the PC to go to, or some place the PC meets her clan. I figure if I'm going to create such a place, I want to be able to use it to tell stories that I otherwise wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T18:38:28-07:00","id":1550135,"title":"","content":"I did do a game set in NYC that had a functioning subway system made up of salvaged bits of the old abandoned lines and stations. Not sure how feasible that is outside of certain cities though. <br /> <br /> It also had the &quot;alleymen&quot;, a gang/cult of homeless rogue ghouls who hunted vampires (borrowed from Requiem), as well as certain urban legend style creatures that were resistant to Animalism for one reason or another (mutation or what have you). Mostly drawing influence from films like Alligator, CHUD, Mimic, and Relic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T02:58:29-07:00","id":1550143,"title":"","content":"Some random points I remember:<br /> <br /> I'm a big advocate of warrens with a fungal garden, if only to convey a sense of Clan culture. Players may not use it as a resource, but it is a good set piece. In the same vein, some communal areas that emphasize the Clan as a whole instead of the specific warren help with that - something that allows easy communication with other Clan members or warrens, a library with book exchange, a 'war room', that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Having a private property in control of the Clan above the inner warren limits visits of city maintenance crews to the more sensitive parts. There should be some thought put into what's directly above.<br /> <br /> Don't skip on modern infrastructure: server room, generator, access to mundane communication nodes etc.<br /> <br /> In terms of traps, it's surprisingly difficult to come up with something that is smart enough not to spring on the wrong person. Especially on the outer perimeter where you don't want the attention caused by a worker falling into a spike pit, so it's better to put deterrents there. Fungi with harmful spores or gas irritants seemed to work well - anything that makes people want to go away and doesn't seem too out of place. Animalism is the second line (rat swarms, spawning pool creatures), and the lethal traps should be confined to the inner warren.<br /> <br /> Generally I prefer warrens as a safe space for Nosferatu, so putting in a 'hunter' of sorts seemed the wrong direction for me. Closest I got to that was warren residents telling newcomers and visitors the story of the Elder Who Sleeps In a Forgotten Secret Room and may awake hungry at any moment. Just a scary bed time story, right? But overall, the Nictuku fill that role already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T04:30:08-07:00","id":1550148,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s also interesting to wonder if Warrens are ever built into natural cave systems or are built into \u2018ghost towns\u2019 as well as living cities (Assuming those ghost towns are situated in regions still populous enough to sustain at least a small vampiric population).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, one feature I can easily imagine being built into a Warren is a \u2018Rogues Gallery\u2019 put together from images or icons of the local \u2018Beautiful People\u2019 who have somehow cropped up on the Nosferatu Radar (Whether as future Cleopatras or simply as jerks the Nossies want to scribble all over by way of therapy).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also possible to imagine some Warrens putting together a \u2018Grace of God\u2019 gallery - containing images of things that make the residents feel lucky by comparison (Probably images of the high and mighty making monkeys out of themselves, in the main).<br /> <br /> Bonus points if the Warren can find dirt that puts a character from the former into the latter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T04:34:02-07:00","id":1550149,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s a question: where do the Nosferatu set themselves up when there\u2019s no \u2018undercity\u2019 per se? (I.E. where the ground is too swampy to allow extensive digging).<br /> <br /> I have this image of a deserted high-rise being turned into a vertical warren for a start, but one could also imagine a deserted theme park having some appeal (Somewhere that feeds the Nossies schadenfreude would definitely be appropriate to a Clan with it\u2019s roots in German horror movies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T11:44:36-07:00","id":1550161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550135#post1550135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also had the &quot;alleymen&quot;, a gang/cult of homeless rogue ghouls who hunted vampires (borrowed from Requiem), as well as certain urban legend style creatures that were resistant to Animalism for one reason or another (mutation or what have you). Mostly drawing influence from films like Alligator, CHUD, Mimic, and Relic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting. The Revised Clanbook mentioned the possibility of &quot;subhuman&quot; ghouls whose exposure to Nosferatu vitae eventually made them unable to function on the surface and who lived underground, and that some would become cannibals and eaters of the dead, clearly mirroring Lovecraft's ghouls and films like CHUD.<br /> <br /> It also made mention of possible subhuman ghouls who somehow developed immunity to the blood bond and began hunting vampires on their own. So not quite the same as urban legend animals resistant to Animalism, but in the same vein.<br /> <br /> The clanbook mentioned that such reports were unverified, but then gave mechanics. Typical wink-wink type stuff of ideas that are not strictly canon, but leaving it up to the ST if they want to include them in their game.<br /> <br /> I'd like to include something mysterious and possibly dangerous in the warrens that the Nosferatu NPCs can't confirm or control, but want to make it acceptable to my players. If I include Vhujunka or Flying Polyps, it might break their genre expectations. Some ghouled animal that broke free and is on the loose might make a good compromise. Maybe some enormous boa constrictor who could potentially swallow and eat an entire Kindred/ghoul/mortal.<br /> <br /> I might also include some of your &quot;alleymen&quot; - abandoned, &quot;rogue&quot; ghouls - who try using parts of that subterranean infrastructure as hideouts as they search for vitae, and the local Nosferatu may need to periodically eliminate them in order to prevent outsiders from exploring too much of the warrens and obtaining useful information. Maybe such ghouls are desperate enough to try and find the spawning pools so they can get their fix. A PC can respond to this in many different ways so it might make a good dilemma for them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T12:07:57-07:00","id":1550165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550149#post1550149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here\u2019s a question: where do the Nosferatu set themselves up when there\u2019s no \u2018undercity\u2019 per se? (I.E. where the ground is too swampy to allow extensive digging).</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the entire existence of a warren, and its associated features, is more of an ideal or commonality of the clan rather than an essential requirement. in Chicago By Night, Khalid's haven was in some cave north of Evanston, IL, not somewhere underground in Chicago, and it was said this was where the clan usually meets. Then again, Chicago By Night was written before the information we'd get in the Players Guides or Clanbooks, so not everything matches to later &quot;expectations&quot; of players.<br /> <br /> Your ideas of abandoned places are good. I also think that certain areas of the wilderness also work. If there is a nearby swamp, that could easily fulfill most of the same function as a &quot;classic&quot; constructed warren. It's something most people and Kindred would avoid. It has lots of dangers and pitfalls. Plenty of critters that could become monstrous. And Kindred could easily burrow deep enough to avoid the sun. It's probably the &quot;original&quot; warren.<br /> <br /> My head canon is that Grendel and his dam of Beowulf fame are wilderness dwelling Nosferatu so I often fall back to their lairs as examples of how Nosferatu survive in the wilderness.<br /> <br /> Now there is some potential of Gangrel or Lupines intruding, but they aren't found everywhere, and both can mitigated in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T12:40:09-07:00","id":1550170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550143#post1550143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a big advocate of warrens with a fungal garden, if only to convey a sense of Clan culture. Players may not use it as a resource, but it is a good set piece.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting flavor. It could make an interesting hobby for an NPC that otherwise lacks flair or spark or who makes a limited contribution to the warren.<br /> <br /> Your other ideas are also all good, and I'm entering them in my notes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550143#post1550143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally I prefer warrens as a safe space for Nosferatu, so putting in a 'hunter' of sorts seemed the wrong direction for me. Closest I got to that was warren residents telling newcomers and visitors the story of the Elder Who Sleeps In a Forgotten Secret Room and may awake hungry at any moment. Just a scary bed time story, right? But overall, the Nictuku fill that role already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it is supposed to be a safe space, and I don't want to take that away from them or the PC. But there is also a general sense of the Nosferatu digging too deep and uncovering strange things, and a general sense of paranoia. Most players will realize the Nictuku won't be showing up in a normal chronicle so they're relegated to interesting lore that have no impact in the setting. Even good roleplayers can't help be motivated by metaknowledge of the setting.<br /> <br /> However, if I have something <i>else</i> that is unknown that has obviously entered the environment, then the player's imagination will take over. And I'd rather have in mind something real present down there than just some unknown Mystery Box level BS that I make up all the time. Something that can leave some kind of trace evidence - tracks, sounds, cast off materials, spoor, etc - but which can't be easily identified.<br /> <br /> A &quot;hunter&quot; in this case does not need to be someone actually hunting and destroying Nosferatu. Just something down there with the Nosferatu that they don't control which can feed into the clan's natural paranoia. But something a PC could conceivably find trace of, hunt for, and eventually encounter if they wanted. Then based on what it is, the PC (and clan) can decide what to do about it - destroy it, negotiate with it, ignore it, change the design of the warren, etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T14:28:27-07:00","id":1550176,"title":"","content":"I feel like there should be some sort of Archive room, a place where the lore keepers store records, tomes, and other items of interest or importance. This may also double as a place where collected blackmail materials are kept. Perhaps some sort of adjacent area where people (Nosferatu, ghouls, whatever) are careful reassembling shredded documents, recording phone calls, etc. This may or may not include computers and hackers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-16T01:03:42-07:00","id":1550187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550170#post1550170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, if I have something <i>else</i> that is unknown that has obviously entered the environment, then the player's imagination will take over. And I'd rather have in mind something real present down there than just some unknown Mystery Box level BS that I make up all the time. Something that can leave some kind of trace evidence - tracks, sounds, cast off materials, spoor, etc - but which can't be easily identified.<br /> <br /> A &quot;hunter&quot; in this case does not need to be someone actually hunting and destroying Nosferatu. Just something down there with the Nosferatu that they don't control which can feed into the clan's natural paranoia. But something a PC could conceivably find trace of, hunt for, and eventually encounter if they wanted. Then based on what it is, the PC (and clan) can decide what to do about it - destroy it, negotiate with it, ignore it, change the design of the warren, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, so basically 'spiders': the spiders aren't interested in people, they are just there to catch food - they may be even beneficial, if they prey on pests. At the same time, people don't want to stick their fingers into dark corners or they will catch a bite. I could see that work. Going with the analogy, my pick would be some ethereal entity/entities that have gathered around a resource that happens to be in the same place.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's a small Node. Some kind of umbrood has settled to feed off its energy, keeping the levels low enough so it flies under the radar of third parties with magic aptitude. They ignore the Nosferatu unless they poke their food source unwittingly - say, by using a Discipline inside the warren or disturb the feng shui of the place. If they do there could be some 'warning gesture', ie poltergeisty things happening. At the same time they would keep other unwanted umbral visitors out of the area. Come to think of it, Pattern Spiders might not be the worst choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 04-16-2025, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-16T12:02:56-07:00","id":1550195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550176#post1550176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like there should be some sort of Archive room, a place where the lore keepers store records, tomes, and other items of interest or importance. This may also double as a place where collected blackmail materials are kept. Perhaps some sort of adjacent area where people (Nosferatu, ghouls, whatever) are careful reassembling shredded documents, recording phone calls, etc. This may or may not include computers and hackers.</div> </div> </div> </div> It amuses me to imagine some raging arguments over who gets to clean up all this miscellany if it proves useless and even bigger arguments about where to store all this clutter should it prove potentially useful (I.E. \u2018Not actually useful YET).<br /> <br /> \u2018Nosferatu Pack Rat\u2019 and \u2018Nosferatu De-clutter\u2019 are character concepts I can actually imagine somebody running with (or at least developing as NPCs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-16T15:48:28-07:00","id":1550202,"title":"","content":"Curious as if there are good defenses to things like astral projectors and ghosts spying on or exploring the warrens? With enough patience, such beings would be able to see through Obfuscate and eventually follow a Nosferatu heading towards the warren. It seems to me that most warrens won't have anything, and the Nosferatu will just need to accept that this is always a gap in their defenses.<br /> <br /> There's always the alternative to use some sort of blood magic ritual that prevents that, but I think it'd only be the very rare warren that has something like that.<br /> <br /> However, if there are things like tinfoil hat or thin sheet of lead can prevent that kind of intrusion or scrying (perhaps not effective against everything), then I think many warrens would know to incorporate that into any kind of construction.<br /> <br /> There's also the possibility of other kind of reprisals. Like if the local brood discovered such a thing and recognized the person responsible, then they'd freeze that person out of any future information sharing, and alert other broods to do the same. Or if they have friends or allies with similar powers, to ask them to intervene on their behalf. If so, they might want to cultivate such &quot;friends&quot; so they can call in such favors.<br /> <br /> Likewise the issue with animal spies. Other Kindred with Animalism could potentially do that as could Lupines. Of course, such animals would likely be eaten by the creatures of the spawning pool, so that may just be good enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-16T21:44:08-07:00","id":1550203,"title":"","content":"Most storm-drains and sewers, are one way; that is, they rarely split up and it's impossible to get lost. Though, there are many, smaller-tunnels, but they are also one-way. I know; I've been in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T01:47:48-07:00","id":1550207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550202#post1550202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious as if there are good defenses to things like astral projectors and ghosts spying on or exploring the warrens? With enough patience, such beings would be able to see through Obfuscate and eventually follow a Nosferatu heading towards the warren. It seems to me that most warrens won't have anything, and the Nosferatu will just need to accept that this is always a gap in their defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Havens have this particular weakness, and I tend to leave it in as an advantage for Tremere and Giovanni to exploit. As long as the ST doesn't abuse it for an uncalled umbral surprise attack from a werewolf pack, it usually doesn't come into play unless the players get involved with one of the two Clans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550202#post1550202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's always the alternative to use some sort of blood magic ritual that prevents that, but I think it'd only be the very rare warren that has something like that.<br /> <br /> However, if there are things like tinfoil hat or thin sheet of lead can prevent that kind of intrusion or scrying (perhaps not effective against everything), then I think many warrens would know to incorporate that into any kind of construction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's conceivable for Nosferatu in particular that they could reach out to the Clan and ask for a member who is proficient in blood magic to ward their warren. It's probably expensive, not quick, and nothing I would assume as a default.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's an influence from the old Vampire TV show, but I always liked Nosferatu who dabbled in Alchemy. Maybe there is something that could tie in with the fungal gardens - like a potion that makes it possible to create spawning pool creatures able to peer into the penumbra, or something similar.<br /> <br /> There is also folk magic for the tinfoil hat approach (I think it's detailed in one of the Dark Ages supplements) that would allow minimal securities like a spirit trap that snaps if 'something' has trespassed. I would keep those effects to 'barely working, hardly informative' though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T10:12:18-07:00","id":1550216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550207#post1550207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Havens have this particular weakness, and I tend to leave it in as an advantage for Tremere and Giovanni to exploit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and that is fine. I just want to make sure I think things through beforehand and don't miss anything &quot;obvious&quot;. There's always the possibility someone is reading the thread and shouting, &quot;What, you don't know about wrapping a wet towel around your head?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KAP-FQblfYI\" data-code=\"KAP-FQblfYI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/KAP-FQblfYI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550207#post1550207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as the ST doesn't abuse it for an uncalled umbral surprise attack from a werewolf pack, it usually doesn't come into play unless the players get involved with one of the two Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I'd ever do that. Not only would players scream about it being unfair (I agree), I actually don't think that's a very viable option. There should be a fairly strong gauntlet in such areas, meaning the tactic might not only fail but put Garou at risk, but also that such places likely attracts hostile Banes or other spirits that mean it would be dangerous for the Garou to simply travel there in the Penumbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550207#post1550207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe there is something that could tie in with the fungal gardens - like a potion that makes it possible to create spawning pool creatures able to peer into the penumbra, or something similar.<br /> <br /> There is also folk magic for the tinfoil hat approach (I think it's detailed in one of the Dark Ages supplements) that would allow minimal securities like a spirit trap that snaps if 'something' has trespassed. I would keep those effects to 'barely working, hardly informative' though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just occurred to me that for ghosts at least, there are some obvious defenses. <br /> <br /> Aura Perception does detect the auras of wraiths. Someone untrained with it might not realize it is a wraith, but seeing any aura that is not associated with an obvious body would create suspicion. It's not a typical Nosferatu power as it is an out of clan Discipline, but many warrens could have someone who knows that power. Many long established warrens could have learned the benefit of this from visitors of other broods. It could easily be something of a checklist of standard Nosferatu knowledge of warren defense.<br /> <br /> Forbiddance and Warding does provide some protection. That's always mentioned as something available to living humans so most likely undead vampires should not have access to it. However, ghouls are still living. So Nosferatu may have one or more servants who have enough knowledge to provide it and be trusted enough to allow inside the warren. How common is this done? Probably depends on the domain, but if a local brood decides it's warranted, they probably have enough connection with other broods to find one where it is done and quickly learn what they need to do, or request someone to arrive to perform it while they wait to develop a local resource. It's certainly easier than trying to find a vampire with the appropriate blood magic rituals or necromancy.<br /> <br /> I also believe animals can also perfectly see and hear wraiths as well. I am pretty sure that is established lore, but I can't find a reference after a very quick look through my books. (If anyone knows, please let post it!) Now ordinary humans may not understand why their dog is suddenly barking at nothing, but anyone with Animalism can quickly learn the reason. This is probably the most obvious &quot;defense&quot; and would long be known to the Nosferatu. Probably every warren (or Hosting outside the warren) would have a bright dog or other animal who could provide such warning. Such ghouled pets probably already exist for other obvious reasons so this should be a default.<br /> <br /> Now what the brood can do about such things after detection is a different matter. It could just be a normal ghost without connection to the Giovanni, other vampires, or other enemies. Maybe even an entity they could befriend. There may not be any obvious suspects of who in the domain sent the ghost to spy on them. But if this is something they detect on an ongoing basis, at least they could begin investigating how to deal with the perceived threat.<br /> <br /> I don't think there are any similar measures against an astral projector whether the be vampire, mage, or human with numina or sorcery. But there are some things you can't help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T11:44:15-07:00","id":1550220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550216#post1550216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I'd ever do that. Not only would players scream about it being unfair (I agree), I actually don't think that's a very viable option. There should be a fairly strong gauntlet in such areas, meaning the tactic might not only fail but put Garou at risk, but also that such places likely attracts hostile Banes or other spirits that mean it would be dangerous for the Garou to simply travel there in the Penumbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was years ago and there was OOC stuff between the ST and the player, so I don't want you to think it was directed at you. It just came to mind as a bad example for involving the umbra in Vampire games where it is mostly ignored.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550216#post1550216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also believe animals can also perfectly see and hear wraiths as well. I am pretty sure that is established lore, but I can't find a reference after a very quick look through my books. (If anyone knows, please let post it!) Now ordinary humans may not understand why their dog is suddenly barking at nothing, but anyone with Animalism can quickly learn the reason. This is probably the most obvious &quot;defense&quot; and would long be known to the Nosferatu. Probably every warren (or Hosting outside the warren) would have a bright dog or other animal who could provide such warning. Such ghouled pets probably already exist for other obvious reasons so this should be a default.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same thought when I typed out that idea, but wasn't sure. I just checked, it's in the WtO Core (including Wr20):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not everyone is susceptible to the Fog. Children and animals by and large are immune to its effects, perhaps because they don\u2019t comprehend or fear death. Cats in particular are known for watching wraiths through the Shroud, and for reacting in unexpected ways to their presence in the Skinlands. </div> </div> </div>It's a use of Animalism I have frankly never considered. Very interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550216#post1550216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there are any similar measures against an astral projector whether the be vampire, mage, or human with numina or sorcery. But there are some things you can't help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think Obfuscate might work. It targets the mind of a potential watcher, so it seems reasonable that a 'mental projection' would be equally affected. It's not a long term solution, but Obfuscate 5 and 6 could at least proof sensitive meetings against scrying or astral projections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 04-18-2025, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T11:45:33-07:00","id":1550221,"title":"","content":"You could have an Ethereal Filcher down there as a Bygone of sorts.<br /> <br /> It's a D&amp;D creature that wanders in the Ethereal Plane, but is actually just a beast slightly more intelligent than a common animal. It uses the Ethereal as a hiding spot while hunting for food and baubles (it is a magpie of sorts), but its actual nest is material.<br /> <br /> The overall idea is simple and versatile. The monster can be as tough as you need, and its ability to wander through the Umbra or similar makes for a hard investigation. Being a trinket snatcher it can either get something from the Nos, or have something the Nos want. Yet while it may be extremely disturbing to have around, it isn't really a lethal threat if left alone.<br /> <br /> For traps, you need three types: gas/spore clouds that can put humans to sleep or worse without losing precious blood, alarms that detect the presence of undead intruders preferably hours before they arrive, and anything that makes a fight against ghouled animals more difficult. That way those traps mean nothing for members of the clan, and can help a lot even if they aren't deadly by themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T13:32:23-07:00","id":1550226,"title":"","content":"One possible defense against psychic/spiritual/mystic intrusion would be to draw on some of the stuff from The Transylvania Chronicles to have a tradition of Nosferatu builders with ties to the old stone masons and all the assorted mystical mythology that grew up around the Freemasons. This would potentially include secret signs and sigils incorporated into the warren that confuse, distort, or block attempts at scrying and the like. Possibly stuff derived from sacred architecture as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T18:20:33-07:00","id":1550231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550221#post1550221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could have an Ethereal Filcher down there as a Bygone of sorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got me thinking that it'd be easy to put some kind of &quot;ghost&quot; down there that the Nosferatu know &quot;haunts&quot; the warren. Of course, the &quot;ghost&quot; could be anything - a wraith, a rat gaffling spirit, a plasmic creature, bygone, or anything else. It's not hostile and it's never seen. But it is sometimes heard and is blamed whenever something is &quot;misplaced&quot; or &quot;bad luck&quot; happens. So to the Nosferatu, they call it a ghost. Mentions of it is mostly just flavor text, but the ST should have something specific in mind in case an enterprising PC manages to investigate and discover it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550221#post1550221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For traps, you need three types: gas/spore clouds that can put humans to sleep or worse without losing precious blood,</div> </div> </div> </div>There are lots of hazardous sewage gases that can easily be used so most mortals avoid certain spots entirely. Hydrogen sulfide, carbon dioxide, methane, ammonia. They can knock out or even kill people. I was planning on simply utilizing that for the sewer system access points to the warren, but the Nosferatu could easily collect and divert that gas to other places.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550221#post1550221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">alarms that detect the presence of undead intruders preferably hours before they arrive, and anything that makes</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly motion detector sensors could be easily used. They've existed for a long time, and it wouldn't be hard to install them in certain spots of the warren. If people have other specific examples of actual alarms, I'd like to hear them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550221#post1550221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a fight against ghouled animals more difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good, but I'm not sure what kind of things that might be. There's your standard pit traps, spiked pit traps, beartraps, snares, and deadfalls. Fairly easy to install. You can probably train ghouled animals to avoid them. Place them near the animals so when they go off, they hamper movement and give the ghouled animals more of an edge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550221#post1550221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That way those traps mean nothing for members of the clan, and can help a lot even if they aren't deadly by themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>These kinds of traps rarely destroy vampires, but they would weaken them as they damage health levels, consume vitae, and possibly maim limbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T18:30:00-07:00","id":1550232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550226#post1550226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One possible defense against psychic/spiritual/mystic intrusion would be to draw on some of the stuff from The Transylvania Chronicles to have a tradition of Nosferatu builders with ties to the old stone masons and all the assorted mystical mythology that grew up around the Freemasons. This would potentially include secret signs and sigils incorporated into the warren that confuse, distort, or block attempts at scrying and the like. Possibly stuff derived from sacred architecture as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that makes great flavor text, but I'd probably never have that work by itself. It would actually need to be part of some kind of ritual of warding and thus require blood magic for vampires (or the equivalent for sorcerers). Still, referencing &quot;the Ritual of Zelios&quot; or the &quot;works of Zelios&quot; or similar phrasing could be cool in and of itself.<br /> <br /> I might very well include pseduo-masonic signs and sigils in parts of the warren, but they'd have zero mechanical effect. They might still cause an intruder to fear that something may happen, as many astral projectors would likely have enough occult knowledge to recognize what those signs may mean. Or if they don't know what they mean, they may still freak out. If you can convince someone to turn back, it works as a deterrence even if it really cannot do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T19:01:20-07:00","id":1550233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550220#post1550220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just checked, it's in the WtO Core (including Wr20):</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! It was in the Fog section! That was one place I didn't look.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550220#post1550220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a use of Animalism I have frankly never considered. Very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither did I until I started thinking about because of your comment. It makes a very low effort defense against ghosts at least. Once you realize it, the obviousness of it probably means the Nosferatu have been using it for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550220#post1550220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think Obfuscate might work. It targets the mind of a potential watcher, so it seems reasonable that a 'mental projection' would be equally affected. It's not a long term solution, but Obfuscate 5 and 6 could at least proof sensitive meetings against scrying or astral projections.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had thought about this too. However, after I reviewed Obfuscate 5, I realized it wouldn't work. First, it only covers enough people up to one's Stealth ability. So maybe small groups of Nosferatu, but most broods would probably be too large. Also, the entire cloak drops for everyone if even one person exposes himself, and speaking is a violation of Unseen Presence. So it's not going to be a useful defense to prevent someone spying on the group. At best it could just hide who might be down there at any one time.<br /> <br /> Now it could theoretically work to hide a Nosferatu going to the warrens and preventing a person discovering the entrance and a safe passage to its center by following them. Except any vampire with Auspex 5 can automatically pierce the Obfuscate of most Nosferatu and has a good chance of beating even a Nosferatu with Obfuscate 5.<br /> <br /> Of course, an Obfuscate 6+ power could make this idea work. However, that is probably an exceptional case. Khalid in Chicago By Night can obfuscate an entire place and people in it even if he is not present, and does this to protect the clan meeting place (a large cave outside Evanston). Great if the warren has someone of that power, but I think most warrens probably would not.<br /> <br /> Such things might be possible in V5 or Requiem style rules, but I've never read those and can't comment. I know they are different from classic VtM rules.<br /> <br /> Against things like Garou spying from the Penumbra, it would work much better. But there are probably other things keeping a Garou away from the Penumbra of a warren. It could also work against non-vampires astral projecting whose power sets might be set up differently than Auspex, and thus their Obfuscate might beat it because their actual awareness is still lower.<br /> <br /> But this is all a good discussion. Lots of people are making some very good points on this thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T19:18:41-07:00","id":1550234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550232#post1550232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that makes great flavor text, but I'd probably never have that work by itself. It would actually need to be part of some kind of ritual of warding and thus require blood magic for vampires (or the equivalent for sorcerers). Still, referencing &quot;the Ritual of Zelios&quot; or the &quot;works of Zelios&quot; or similar phrasing could be cool in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be one of those rituals (developed by Zelios or someone similar) that draws power from the vitae used but isn't full Thaumaturgy, similar to the Hedge Magic rules in the original Storytellers Handbook (page 118). Something that probably requires at least 4 dots in Occult with a specialization in Rituals and maybe 3 or more dots in Clan Lore (to have heard of Zelios and know about his work), with the sigils made from the creator's vitae and needing X blood points worth to effect Y amount of space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T23:39:49-07:00","id":1550235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550234#post1550234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be one of those rituals (developed by Zelios or someone similar) that draws power from the vitae used but isn't full Thaumaturgy, similar to the Hedge Magic rules in the original Storytellers Handbook (page 118).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! You are really going into the Wayback Machine for this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D-QM00ABzfk\" data-code=\"D-QM00ABzfk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/D-QM00ABzfk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> For those who don't own the original 1992 sourcebook, its &quot;Hedge Magic&quot; is basically a way to cast individual &quot;spells&quot; or &quot;rituals&quot;. It's not like the normal Paths of vampire Thaumaturgy or human Sorcery. Do I really want a way for PCs to cast rituals/spells outside of knowing some actual form of blood magic? At the time, it was probably intended as way for individual characters to know some form of magic while reserving &quot;true&quot; vampire magick for just the Tremere. The subsequent explosion of non-Tremere blood magic since 1992 should render that approach obsolete.<br /> <br /> It's not exactly clear to me if the RAW apply to vampires as well as mortals, but it's arguably so. I would say those rules are probably well obsolete for anyone wanting to run anything outside exclusively 1e rules, but I have to give you points for both rules mastery and imagination. Special kudos for actually providing the mechanics to do it!<br /> <br /> While I think that the original Storyteller's Handbook is completely obsolete, I must admit there are things in it that I love that really haven't been repeated in subsequent sourcebooks. It's very much a toolbox to allow you to run the kind of game you want rather than the railroad metaplot one-true-way sourcebooks that came later. It's one of the special things that make early edition so inspiring. So I do steal liberally from it, but perhaps not this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 04-18-2025, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T08:50:51-07:00","id":1550239,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the original STH is full of so much wonderful esoteric weirdness. Not just stuff like hedge magic or faeries, but also stuff like rules for embezzling money and riding horses (not at the same time), expanded hunting guidelines, and a bunch of song suggestions.<br /> <br /> It occurs to me that it would have been interesting back in the day to see a bunch of vampire hedge magic rituals that drew on the powers of vitae by requiring the user have a Discipline at a specific level (the above one needing Obfuscate at, say, 5, for example). The sort of thing that would have allowed non-elders to have unique Discipline tricks without needing 6+ ratings, as well as allowing different Clans to have their own secret exploits that put different spins on shared Disciplines. The Brujah, Toreador, and Ventrue all having different rituals for Presence, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T09:15:14-07:00","id":1550241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550239#post1550239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that it would have been interesting back in the day to see a bunch of vampire hedge magic rituals that drew on the powers of vitae by requiring the user have a Discipline at a specific level (the above one needing Obfuscate at, say, 5, for example). The sort of thing that would have allowed non-elders to have unique Discipline tricks without needing 6+ ratings, as well as allowing different Clans to have their own secret exploits that put different spins on shared Disciplines. The Brujah, Toreador, and Ventrue all having different rituals for Presence, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ritual use of Disciplines has some legs in later editions too, most prominently in Abyss Mysticism for Obtenebration. Arguably the more specialized use cases of Discipline powers like creating vozhd or szlachta with Vicissitude also fall into this category. It's probably something that would have been more developed if blood sorcery didn't expand as it did, most likely with the revision of Necromancy and adjacent Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T10:42:16-07:00","id":1550242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550231#post1550231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds good, but I'm not sure what kind of things that might be. There's your standard pit traps, spiked pit traps, beartraps, snares, and deadfalls. Fairly easy to install. You can probably train ghouled animals to avoid them. Place them near the animals so when they go off, they hamper movement and give the ghouled animals more of an edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything that hinders movement is a good start. You can also think about the anatomy of the animals near a given trap, as that may make something hard for a normal humanoid body to pass by, but some animals go through no problem. For example something simple like a tangle of ropes from waist size and above, forcing intruders to crawl. Also you can reduce visibility with mist or darkness where you have animals that don't rely a lot on sight, like bats or specially trained dogs.<br /> <br /> The problem with traps that do actual harm is that you should always consider the inhabitants and possible accidents. Be it someone coming back drunk from laced blood or just having to move around during the day, even just a forgetful moment or a misstep, relying on people just not triggering the trap isn't a good policy, you need to have a contingency for allies falling to the trap. If the trap just hamper movement or sight, counting on animals to do the actual harming, then it is just a small inconvenience for any resident going through it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550232#post1550232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that makes great flavor text, but I'd probably never have that work by itself. It would actually need to be part of some kind of ritual of warding and thus require blood magic for vampires (or the equivalent for sorcerers). Still, referencing &quot;the Ritual of Zelios&quot; or the &quot;works of Zelios&quot; or similar phrasing could be cool in and of itself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think with the current &quot;bloat&quot; of Blood Magic, it wouldn't be too out there for the Nos to have their own Path of Warding. A single Path bought as Out of Clan and focused on making wards for the warren, with a small list of warding rituals. It wouldn't greatly change the clan, but would be far simpler to have at least one member per warren (or at least per big warren and many, but not all, minor ones) that has it. I personally think that the &quot;bloat&quot; was a good idea in the end.<br /> <br /> Other interesting option is to have those rituals as a Combo Discipline. They're easily forgotten, but are actually a very good mechanic that should be in the core since Revised. Combos between Obfuscate and whatever you deem fit should easily provide specific niche powers to ward the warren against more arcane threats like Auspex and unwelcome spirits. You can justify this combo with Potence or Animalism to make it easier for the clan to develop, but having one or two members that Combo with Auspex shouldn't be really hard, and the secret of those Combos would still be with the clan.<br /> <br /> Both methods are within the current V20 rules and would let you have wards against spiritual/astral incursions at lower power levels, easier to justify in any warren.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T14:47:11-07:00","id":1550249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550242#post1550242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example something simple like a tangle of ropes from waist size and above, forcing intruders to crawl.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550242#post1550242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with traps that do actual harm is that you should always consider the inhabitants and possible accidents.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Since there's usually talk of a &quot;maze&quot; or &quot;labyrinth&quot; in the warrens, I imagine that there are paths that are meant to be used by the Nosferatu themselves. These are relatively safe, but more hidden than others. There may be no obstacles here, or obstacles like you described that hinder or delay movement, but do no damage. <br /> <br /> Then there are paths meant for non-Nosferatu. The Nosferatu do not enter those except for those paths they &quot;safely&quot; escort a non-Nosferatu to the antechamber. All the other paths are dangerous as they're just meant to stop intruders trying to invade. These would lead to harmful traps, dead ends, obstacles, spawning pool animals, and the like. The only time the Nosferatu enter these would be to repair or reset traps, and there would be some kind of safety protocol involved. Other STs can run it differently, but that will probably be my default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550242#post1550242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think with the current &quot;bloat&quot; of Blood Magic, it wouldn't be too out there for the Nos to have their own Path of Warding. A single Path bought as Out of Clan and focused on making wards for the warren, with a small list of warding rituals. It wouldn't greatly change the clan, but would be far simpler to have at least one member per warren (or at least per big warren and many, but not all, minor ones) that has it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is certainly an option. I would probably select the actual Path of Warding described in the Dark Ages Companion. It's something I'd argue that Zelios might be able to discover on his own, and then tie in several warding rituals and the like with it. They are the secrets of the Craft of Zelios or whatever you want to call it.<br /> <br /> If I went this route, I'd make any Nosferatu who knew it to be part of some secret craftmason society within the Nosferatu exclusively made up of stonemasons/engineers interested in sacred geometry. It would be very similar to Freemasonry, but it's own thing and very much inline with the legendry associated with the more spiritual or occult aspects of cathedral construction that go back to the Temple of Solomon. As such, it's not simply meant to be a practical teaching, but something designed to spiritually elevate its members. Therefore, the number of Nosferatu who know it are very rare. They essentially need to join a guild, learn its rules, work on its degrees, take vows not to reveal its secrets, etc. I would prefer it if only a rare few warrens would have such defenses, and like other wards they don't always work or cover only some places or times.<br /> <br /> Keeping it limited also provides an ST with the option of using it as a story for their PCs. If there's not simply an NPC already there doing it at every warren, then it can become a plot point where a PC decides to visit to another brood and request help, or joining the order and becoming an apprentice, dealing with politics within the masonic organization, finding out ways to provide boons so such a mason would show up and begin placing some wards in your warren, etc. It creates more plots and stories.<br /> <br /> I actually don't want Nosferatu warrens to be invulnerable anymore than I want Tremere chantries to be invulnerable or any other lair/haven/place (whether individual or communal) to be invulnerable. I think it's perfectly fine to have warrens be vulnerable to someone with Auspex 5. It's an advanced power, and players who work their way to it should be able to get some use out of it. I don't like simply saying, &quot;No, the warrens are supposed to be invulnerable and the Nosferatu meetings secret, so there...&quot; I just like thinking it through before games begin so I can determine that this is a vulnerability you just have to accept. Or if it turns out to be something like ghosts where we figured out there may be some easy things to do to mitigate it, even if it cannot be eliminated.<br /> <br /> Rather than letting characters use astral projection without consequences, or arbitrarily screwing them over so it becomes useless, I'd rather have some idea of complications, threats, obstacles, diversions, or other opportunities arise so it is not simply an auto-win. But that's a larger question in regards to the use of that power and what exactly the astral plane in Vampire should be, not something limited to its use against the warrens. I do have some ideas on that, so I'll just need to review my notes and ponder what other things might happen to astral travelers while they are on their way to the warrens or any other place.<br /> <br /> However, every ST and gaming group has different tastes, and if this is the route they want to go down, more power to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550242#post1550242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think that the &quot;bloat&quot; was a good idea in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of two minds on that. I do like that there's an acknowledgment of other blood magic traditions outside the Tremere. Their exclusive monopoly of it created problems IC and OOC. I think it's better that there are more traditions out there while still keeping the setting role of the Tremere possessing far more occult power than any other rival groups. However, there's the potential problem that it makes it seem as if everyone knows blood magic, and the game stops being about vampires and becomes about vampire sorcerers. And that's not the same game. I still want blood magic to be relatively rare, and the magic itself to be secrets that are hard to learn.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T14:43:09-07:00","id":1550292,"title":"","content":"I actually agree with you, I just don't think magical wards should be &quot;instant win buttons&quot;. There's a number of ways how a ward may be in place, but still be possible to pass through:<br /> <br /> 1- It may be resisted, possibly with an alarm triggering if it actually wards off an assailant, maybe just be there;<br /> 2- It may work by causing a penalty or other ill effect, or by marking the passing entity so it can be identified later;<br /> 3- It may be high maintenance, not really being up and running all the time, or maybe the vampire that does maintenance can be dealt with;<br /> 4- It may have weaknesses of sorts. Either blind spots, or maybe some key objects or actions bypass the ward;<br /> 5- It may fave false alarms, specially if it is indeed an alarm system. Timing your entrance with the &quot;ghost&quot; is a way in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T21:33:50-07:00","id":1550356,"title":"","content":"Revised Edition's Clanbook helpfully points out that every modern city has two parallel sewer systems - one that the toilets empty into, and a separate one that takes away rainwater and snowmelt from the storm drains. It's likely that, in most cities, there's your two segregated pathways for member of the clan and for outsiders seeking to petition the warren for business. The clan members know about the cleaner path through the storm drain tunnels.<br /> <br /> Any hills, caves, or tunnels near or under the setting city's real world version can easily be expanded upon to serve the clan's needs in the world of the game, and the Song Of The Dark Animalism power is specifically meant to answer the question of how the clan's elders get the tunneling done.<br /> <br /> The safest place for the warren's sleeping chambers is where no one would think to look, even if they have supernatural senses. Flooded chambers tunneled beneath nearby lakes, rivers, and reservoirs have the added security advantage of being fireproof, just in case.<br /> <br /> One of Onyx Path's supplements for Requiem (I don't recall which, sorry) dropped the incredibly useful hint that a Warren doesn't have to be entirely underground at all. The meeting place where outsiders can approach the clan's leadership or ambassadors could easily be in an office on a high floor downtown. The rest of the warren could be apartments in different buildings scattered across the clan's territory. I quite like the mental image of these creatures capering and gamboling from rooftop to rooftop, assisted by their Potence, unseen thanks to Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> I've only ever seen it mentioned once, in Lore Of The Clans for V20, but the Nosferatu, the Gangrel, and the Tzimisce are the masters of urban pest control. Since only one of these clans has membership in the Camarilla as of the start of Revised Edition, the Nosferatu should have a LOT of leverage if they present a unified front due to their implied ability to threaten or secure a given real estate property's value thanks to their influence over the city's vermin. A warren could turn that into some choice real estate holdings for themselves if they play their cards just right with a Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-23T23:05:25-07:00","id":1550357,"title":"","content":"Many great points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550356#post1550356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any hills, caves, or tunnels near or under the setting city's real world version can easily be expanded upon to serve the clan's needs in the world of the game, and the Song Of The Dark Animalism power is specifically meant to answer the question of how the clan's elders get the tunneling done.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a Revised clanbook embellishment of Song of the Dark. The first clanbook makes no such assertions. It just says it &quot;enables contact with the monstrous denizens of the underworld.&quot; Revised gives one reason why the power might be used. It's a good evocative choice, but like many Revised era descriptions, it unfortunately limits what the power can do. A wise ST can get more mileage out of its more simple 1e description.<br /> <br /> A sixth level Discipline is not out of place for many warrens. 7th generation and stronger Nosferatu will be present in many warrens.<br /> <br /> To me, the question is what kind of &quot;monstrous denizens of the underworld&quot; will best add to a chronicle. It's the kind of thing that can inspire many different kinds of player responses. When I was a much more &quot;purist&quot; player who hated anything outside the typical vampire genre, this is the kind of power I'd roll my eyes over. Now I'm much more open to it provided it still hits that horror nerve. However, if it goes too fantasy, I wouldn't like it. So coming up with specific kinds of creatures might appear, and how they would interact with the Nosferatu is vitally important.<br /> <br /> Simply using the Call of Cthulhu RPG as inspiration, you can go with bog standard ghouls to ghasts to serpent-men to gugs to cthonians. Using other sources, you can have crawlers, thunderwyrms (or graboids), vhujunka, mole people, sleestaks, carnivorous earthworms, worms of the earth, derro, or gormuu. Which one of these (or any other you can think up) &quot;fits&quot; a generic game of vampire? Which creates that sensation of &quot;this is cool, I wonder how this will turn out&quot; versus &quot;why is this crap in my vampire game?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd love to showcase this power in the chronicle, but currently hesitant until I know the kind of creature or creatures this would summon in front of a Nosferatu PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T17:16:10-07:00","id":1550415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550231#post1550231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are lots of hazardous sewage gases that can easily be used so most mortals avoid certain spots entirely. Hydrogen sulfide, carbon dioxide, methane, ammonia. They can knock out or even kill people. I was planning on simply utilizing that for the sewer system access points to the warren, but the Nosferatu could easily collect and divert that gas to other places.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the safe areas of the warren that aren't frequented by ghouls or using equipment requiring combustion, some process producing nitrogen to release into the air could be very effective. Odorless, tasteless, quietly replaces oxygen to asphyxiate air breathers, makes server rooms safe from fires, shouldn't inconvenience Nosferatu at all beyond the extra work of clearing out dead (or unconscious if found quickly enough) people and animals that wander too near. Sadly it won't suppress gunfire since ammo contains its own oxidizer, but intruders expecting to use fire to their advantage would run into a nasty surprise even if they don't need to breathe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T19:27:48-07:00","id":1550420,"title":"","content":"Some places could also be filled with Argon gas, which is preferred for being inert and heavy, easily displacing other gases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550357#post1550357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many great points.<br /> <br /> To me, the question is what kind of &quot;monstrous denizens of the underworld&quot; will best add to a chronicle. It's the kind of thing that can inspire many different kinds of player responses. When I was a much more &quot;purist&quot; player who hated anything outside the typical vampire genre, this is the kind of power I'd roll my eyes over. Now I'm much more open to it provided it still hits that horror nerve. However, if it goes too fantasy, I wouldn't like it. So coming up with specific kinds of creatures might appear, and how they would interact with the Nosferatu is vitally important.</div> </div> </div> </div>The horror/fantasy divide has more to do with variety, frequency and how the creatures are presented, than with the specific creatures used. Choose few options and use them sparingly, and you can probably make most of them hit the horror button without feeling like fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T23:15:32-07:00","id":1550425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550415#post1550415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some process producing nitrogen to release into the air could be very effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm potentially intrigued by this, but the logistician in me wonders in what ways this could be produced. Is it capturing some kind of industrial waste product? Is it a chemical/biological waste product produced by the Nosferatu themselves, and if so how do they do it so I can describe it to the PCs? That may not be necessary to non-Nosferatu. But for the Nosferatu PCs, I need more detail.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to utilize the natural gases produced by a sewer system. It's just a matter of using them as is, or collecting and diverting them. While somewhat difficult in practice, it's easy enough to explain to PCs and handwave the actual effort to do so. Other gases not naturally produced take more time and effort to explain.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea! I just want to bridge theory and practice.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-27T23:54:13-07:00","id":1550427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550420#post1550420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Choose few options and use them sparingly, and you can probably make most of them hit the horror button without feeling like fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do agree with this and feel it is good advice, I still feel the specific creature or creatures selected do matter a great deal.<br /> <br /> First, there is no real time restriction on Song of the Deep. 1e clanbook provides none at all. Revised clanbook suggests once per year for every five Willpower the summoner possesses. So conceivably at least once per year. While for many PCs, this is not too often as multi-year IC chronicles are rare in my experience, but for the warrens in general this can be a fairly frequent occurrence. Even at just an annual basis, this could be a lot for most warrens over the years. It has the potential to not be just &quot;I summon some strange monster to do whatever chaos it can&quot; to &quot;the warren actually has a relationship with these creatures that should be roleplayed.&quot; If the power allows it, I feel &quot;Hey, just don't do it that often&quot; is not a valid response unless the response is to say the power should be restricted to a less common frequency (and then provides what it should be).<br /> <br /> Second, the power is not necessarily limited to animal level intelligence. It is easy to fall into the thinking these should only be animal level creatures. But Animalism is more about the &quot;Beast&quot; than it is about animals. It affects humans and vampires too. So what it summons may not be unintelligent. 1e clanbook even mentions it may alert Nictuku (if botched). The type of creature matters.<br /> <br /> Summoning some unintelligent or at least non-communicative cthonian, graboid, or thunderwyrm is one thing. Summoning an intelligent vhujunka, serpent-men, or Shaver Mystery-style derro is quite another. Vastly different interaction between the monstrous subterranean denizen and the summoner (and thus the warren).<br /> <br /> Third, there is lots of obvious crossover potential. We're leaving strictly vampire territory here for things that are more common in Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, or even Wraith. We should give enough consideration then for this as we would any other crossover. Some crossover elements add to the theme of a vampire game, and others distract.<br /> <br /> This is very much an ST fiat power, especially because normally this is only available to NPCs that are stronger than 8th generation. However, it is so evocative and distinct I do want to use it as part of the clan and warren for PCs. Generic discussion of the power avoids the hard choices an ST needs to make. I understand personal taste can lead to STs making vastly different decisions. Nevertheless, I think it helps everyone to grapple with the differences in its application. <br /> <br /> Someone choosing enormous, but unintelligent beasts is making a different design choice than someone choosing sophisticated, but lonely subterranean survivors like vhujunka, much less a race of beings like Lovecraftian ghouls or crawlers who are intelligent, but lack much civilization. Not to mention classic fairy tale elements like trolls or slumbering dragons. All can be considered equally valid, but the consequences to the chronicle are very different. Even if there is no universal answer, what do people prefer?<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm pedantic, but I prefer to think out these kind of things on this forum than bring it up for the first time in game with the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T11:03:27-07:00","id":1550456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550425#post1550425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm potentially intrigued by this, but the logistician in me wonders in what ways this could be produced.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Common sewer gas contains some nitrogen oxides, along with many other compounds. By itself it will hardly remove all the oxygen in a room, but can still bring it to dangerously low levels all the while filling the air with poisonous gases.<br /> <br /> That's not nitrogen gas <i>per se</i>, though, it is highly reactant and prone to flames and explosions.<br /> <br /> Nitrogen and Argon are commercially available and <i>relatively</i> cheap, they're the main gases used at labs or industrial facilities to displace oxygen. Nitrogen is cheaper (that's one of the reasons for it to be preferred as liquid gas for cooling), but it still reacts with some things, which can have unforeseen effects in the long run. Argon is far more stable and inert, being used when you really need to remove reactants from the air.<br /> <br /> Both gases are good choices for the Nos to fill rooms where they want to keep things, like servers, computers or libraries. Artificial, yes, but perfectly affordable, the room will be devoid of oxygen but otherwise very safe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550427#post1550427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I do agree with this and feel it is good advice, I still feel the specific creature or creatures selected do matter a great deal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The creature chosen does matter, but my point is that how much &quot;fantasy&quot; it gets depends a lot more on how it's used. But indeed, while the setting has them, the mood would be quite different if the thing is a dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T17:54:49-07:00","id":1550530,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure of the process to manufacture it. I know it's used commercially in server rooms and things involving cryogenics, but I'd assume a Nosferatu warren would want to control their own supply if possible rather than be dependent on deliveries of easily tracked big tanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T19:44:47-07:00","id":1550531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550530#post1550530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure of the process to manufacture it. I know it's used commercially in server rooms and things involving cryogenics, but I'd assume a Nosferatu warren would want to control their own supply if possible rather than be dependent on deliveries of easily tracked big tanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>If all they intend is to use it once as an emergency fire suppressant or as an activated option in one room, they might be fine bringing down gas cylinders once or on a rare basis. Stockpile sufficient supplies at everyone's convenience, and wait until you need it if ever. Large gas cylinders will be heavy, but Nosferatu probably have sufficient Potence not to care. It's more an issue of how much time and effort they need to volunteer to bring it down. A limited time that is not repeated very often, you'll probably get compliant volunteers.<br /> <br /> However, if they intend to fill an entire room (or multiple rooms and corridors), then they'll need an ongoing supply. Nobody will want to spend their eternity doing that.<br /> <br /> If they could produce it themselves down in the warrens by themselves, they would still need raw materials and industrial equipment to do it. Whether they are lugging down gas cylinders or production materials/equipment, it'll be a pain in the ass. And don't forget the passages down there may not be designed to lug in any kind of industrial equipment. Even assuming one of the Nosferatu or a ghoul is a sufficient industrial chemist to do so, I don't think production in the warren itself is viable unless everything one needs is already found in the sewers or only needs to be brought down once or very seldom. However, if all you need is local sewer gas and the equivalent of a high school chemistry classroom to produce the quantities you need, then you can do it.<br /> <br /> It all depends if you need this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=70xgdry2TNw\" data-code=\"70xgdry2TNw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/70xgdry2TNw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Or this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jV439la6nnM\" data-code=\"jV439la6nnM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/jV439la6nnM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> An easier solution may be piping it down below from a secure source. Have a warren member arrange to control a small local factory that uses it, then they can pipe it down themselves. If they can control the owner, then they can even take a large percentage of it without worrying about discovery. If there is any kind of oversight or control, then they'd need to limit or disguise the percentage to an acceptable loss rate. Again, depending how much you need on a regular basis will restrict the size of the operation needed to hide siphoning it off.<br /> <br /> Of course building the pipe system to deliver the gas where it needs to be requires some extensive construction work. As would making sure certain rooms or sections can be sealed off sufficiently so you don't lose the gas through leakage. But assuming they already have the construction skills and control of sewer system to build the warren normally, I don't think that would be a problem. It would still be a project, but one not too different from any other work down in the warren. <br /> <br /> Rather than being something older warrens have, I think this would be limited to newer warrens working out the needs of a modern day computer network or thinking about industrial uses, and would be heavily dependent on a local Nosferatu having the required skills, intelligence, and creativity. Such a thing might cause the warren to stand out, and it could take many decades or even over a century before something like this becomes &quot;standard&quot; in most warrens.<br /> <br /> Other option would be that such places are only found in those portions of the &quot;warren&quot; that are above ground. That would eliminate many of the complications of doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-30T20:07:33-07:00","id":1550532,"title":"","content":"Both Nitrogen and Argon are purified from the atmosphere and cost cents per Kg of gas. Many labs and installations use it, it would be simple to have a front or several for the warren buying it as they need it.<br /> <br /> Production isn't unfeasible, but would still use sodium azide or cooling systems that have the same problem of leaving a track. In fact, an underground facility to produce Nitrogen or Argon would be easier to detect in the long run than a few missing tanks. The methods to purify them use specialized resources, nothing terribly expensive, but traceable none the less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T02:44:34-07:00","id":1550535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550531#post1550531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An easier solution may be piping it down below from a secure source. Have a warren member arrange to control a small local factory that uses it, then they can pipe it down themselves. If they can control the owner, then they can even take a large percentage of it without worrying about discovery. If there is any kind of oversight or control, then they'd need to limit or disguise the percentage to an acceptable loss rate. Again, depending how much you need on a regular basis will restrict the size of the operation needed to hide siphoning it off.<br /> <br /> Of course building the pipe system to deliver the gas where it needs to be requires some extensive construction work. As would making sure certain rooms or sections can be sealed off sufficiently so you don't lose the gas through leakage. But assuming they already have the construction skills and control of sewer system to build the warren normally, I don't think that would be a problem. It would still be a project, but one not too different from any other work down in the warren.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wastewater treatment plant. Provides an ample supply of chlorine, a good cover for why it was built with a sewer connection and 'leaks' that cause elevated chlorine levels in the area. As a bonus, it may even get rid off some of the stink in the warren.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T13:03:20-07:00","id":1550545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550535#post1550535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wastewater treatment plant. Provides an ample supply of chlorine, a good cover for why it was built with a sewer connection and 'leaks' that cause elevated chlorine levels in the area. As a bonus, it may even get rid off some of the stink in the warren.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any benefit to piping in chlorine other than that it is poisonous?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking it may just be better to let elevated levels of carbon dioxide accumulate if you just want to eliminate air breathers as a threat. It's a common hazard in caves. It can be easily created by a variety of natural processes. It's not considered to be odd or suspicious to have high concentrations in subterranean locations. You don't need much more carbon dioxide in the air to cause problems for humans. Fatigue, dizziness, headaches, anxiety, mental slowness and clumsiness all occur at very low levels of concentration. Experienced cavers would leave once they noticed it. Prolonged exposure (which would take place for any mortal exploring the warren) can lead to unconsciousness and likely death. You'll just need to make sure you don't take any human or animal ghouls into those areas.<br /> <br /> Low levels won't do much as a fire suppressant for server rooms, but I'm thinking the warren might only need a few large gas cylinders of nitrogen and argon to provide that. Not something you constantly need to manually bring down or pipe down. And if you don't have a fire, you won't need to replace them. Every so often someone brings down another so you have a stockpile reserve, and it minimizes the effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T15:18:15-07:00","id":1550555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550545#post1550545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any benefit to piping in chlorine other than that it is poisonous?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this would be strictly for deterrent / aggressive use. Having chlorine around a fire is the opposite of a good idea.<br /> <br /> I just liked the cover aspect of it because it's an unattractive target for power players or crooks (as opposed to a chemical plant), and allows for unsuspicious deep construction work around the plant if necessary. If you're looking for multiple benefits of the gas, your idea of using carbon dioxide is better.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T18:12:29-07:00","id":1550561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550545#post1550545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there any benefit to piping in chlorine other than that it is poisonous?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on how you want to model it in the setting as a weapon.<br /> <br /> Chlorine is a particularly nasty poison because it reacts with almost everything a body is made of. So while living beings suffer the most immediate dangers as it attacks the lungs, technically even vampires should be vulnerable to chemical burns from contact with it.<br /> <br /> A room full of chlorine is potentially dangerous (or at least extremely irritating) for undead intruders. Not as much as a room on fire, but still.<br /> <br /> If you want places in the labyrinth that can harm vampires, but remain relatively low profile, your best options are chlorine and methane, the last one with a spark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-01T19:46:17-07:00","id":1550562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550561#post1550561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want places in the labyrinth that can harm vampires, but remain relatively low profile, your best options are chlorine and methane, the last one with a spark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I don't think that's a feature that should appear in all or even most warrens, but it's certainly an option especially if the warren is especially large or the area is considered potentially dangerous for Nosferatu. Or if an ST wants to make this a particular characteristic of the local warren. Then the warren might justify the expense in resources, time, and effort it'll take to make this happen as I think using this would take more than the usual amount of resources.<br /> <br /> However, all this chemical talk makes me think besides the normal Nosferatu archetypes people like to talk about, we obviously missed the one about the Nosferatu chemical engineer. This isn't something you want amateurs doing. It'll take effort to both build and maintain it. You don't want an uncontrolled explosion or leak because you didn't do the proper maintenance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-02T17:33:58-07:00","id":1550613,"title":"","content":"Now I'm imagining some techie Nosferatu fledgling programming drones to project a hologram lightshow of a fiery sewer gas explosion. Scare intruding vampires away in a pinch without subjecting the warren to an actual explosion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T09:03:23-07:00","id":1550690,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, did you ever get around to working up your take on Seattle, Justicar Petrodon\u2019s base of operations? (Seeing an article on BLOODLINES 2 in a video game magazine made me wonder how you would like to see the city depicted in a World of Darkness context).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T18:13:22-07:00","id":1550712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550690#post1550690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, did you ever get around to working up your take on Seattle, Justicar Petrodon\u2019s base of operations? (Seeing an article on BLOODLINES 2 in a video game magazine made me wonder how you would like to see the city depicted in a World of Darkness context).</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's unlikely to be necessary in my LA Free States chronicle. I don't see the players heading there. If they do, I'm sure they'll give me enough time to come up with something. We already have an enormous sandbox as is with LA proper, SoCal, San Francisco, and Phoenix.<br /> <br /> I did live in Seattle at one time and briefly ran a Vampire chronicle set there a long time ago. While I doubt I still have my notes about it, I do have some vague memories of that chronicle and would use that as the basis for the city in this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T23:14:53-07:00","id":1550726,"title":"","content":"To be fair with potance it is not thta hard to dig out a cozy warren of your liking<br /> A bit of how <i>John Henry</i> won duel against a drilling machine, a few shirtless nosferatu with (strong) hammers and Potance<br /> The rest is just logistics<br /> Alex Marshall wrote a book entitled &quot;Beneath the Metropolis: the Secret Lives of Cities&quot;. It covers the subterranean infrastructure, catacombs, sewer systems, rails, etc., of 12 cities, and has provided excellent inspiration for warrens and I shamelessly used it plan Warrens for my stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T03:24:41-07:00","id":1550731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550712#post1550712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. It's unlikely to be necessary in my LA Free States chronicle. I don't see the players heading there. If they do, I'm sure they'll give me enough time to come up with something. We already have an enormous sandbox as is with LA proper, SoCal, San Francisco, and Phoenix.<br /> <br /> I did live in Seattle at one time and briefly ran a Vampire chronicle set there a long time ago. While I doubt I still have my notes about it, I do have some vague memories of that chronicle and would use that as the basis for the city in this one.</div> </div> </div> </div> I admit to being deeply convinced that, given a choice between quiet, practical strategies and swaggering into the dragon\u2019s den threatening to turn old Drake into the world\u2019s most fireproof luggage (All the better to tote out the local hoard of treasure) at least some players will Go Big or Go Home any day of the year (and twice as often on Leap Day).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T22:00:57-07:00","id":1550933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550202#post1550202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious as if there are good defenses to things like astral projectors and ghosts spying on or exploring the warrens? With enough patience, such beings would be able to see through Obfuscate and eventually follow a Nosferatu heading towards the warren. It seems to me that most warrens won't have anything, and the Nosferatu will just need to accept that this is always a gap in their defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know anything to deal with Astral Projectors and other scrying problems, but one potential solution to ghost problems might be a Sluagh friend. Changelings generally don't get along with Vampires that well, given their banality, but the Sluagh tend to encounter Nosferatu a fair bit given their shared affinity for secrets and dark deep damp places. And notably, Sluagh have an innate ability to perceive wraiths. Having a Sluagh ghostbuster on call to deal with hauntings in the warren may not be a universal feature, but if a warren is paranoid enough about ghosts and can find a Sluagh that's got the right arts and doesn't mind dealing with vampiric banality for a bit, they might be a decent solution, certainly most nosferatu would prefer involving an outsider that doesn't have a lot of reason to interact with other vampires compared to hiring a Giovanni to do it (especially if the Giovanni are the reason why they're paranoid about ghosts in their warren in the first place.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24666-ravian","name":"Ravian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T15:53:15-07:00","id":1550948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550127-nosferatu-warren-design?p=1550933#post1550933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know anything to deal with Astral Projectors and other scrying problems, but one potential solution to ghost problems might be a Sluagh friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have given some thoughts about supernatural allies of the Nosferatu, but didn't post them because 1) a lot of players are uneasy about crossover elements, and 2) they're really dependent on local conditions.<br /> <br /> The early sourcebooks often made mention of an information sharing alliance between Nosferatu and Bone Gnawers. CbN gave a Nosferatu the equivalent of Necromany or Spirit Thaumaturgy because of her backstory, though I always felt that might be best simulated through a Medium merit. But the writers used whatever published mechanics they had available at the time. It's fairly easy to justify someone in the warren knowing a single ally that is a medium, sorcerer, sluagh, or whatever that might give them one edge against an unusual intruder.<br /> <br /> Whether players welcome or resent that kind of thing probably changed from game to game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}